Clear
! IEEE 123-Bus Test Feeder — ZT-CARD wrapper (B3 / ztcard-stack #1140)
!
! Loads the Siemens PowerGym 123Bus model (fetched via Dockerfile sparse
! clone) and adds a rooftop PV portfolio for ZT-CARD multi-zone
! experiments. Parallel to Run_IEEE8500_ZTCARD.dss in structure.
!
! The IEEE 123-bus feeder is a ~3.5 MW peak load, 4.16 kV distribution
! circuit with ~120 buses, 7 voltage regulators, 4 shunt capacitors,
! and (from PowerGym) 4 disconnected batteries at buses 33/67/114/300.
! BFS zone partitioning with NUM_RTU_ZONES=5 creates 5 control zones
! for the authorization experiment.
!
! DER portfolio: 25 rooftop PV sites (~75 kW each, 1.875 MW total ≈
! 54% penetration on 3.5 MW peak). Raised from 15 for ztcard-stack #1270 —
! see the zone-fleet block below for why an even per-zone fleet is required
! and what the uneven one broke. Sites are spread across the feeder
! by BFS depth so the data-init zone partitioner distributes them
! across the 5 zones. Buses 33/67/114/300 are intentionally skipped
! (PowerGym's batteries already live there). Each PV is mounted via a
! 100 kVA step-up transformer from 240 V secondary to the 2.4 kV
! line-to-neutral primary on this 4.16 kV system.
!
! PowerGym's standalone SolarRamp.DSS / WindRamp.DSS scripts are NOT
! pulled in — they're OPF-training fixtures (single 2 MW generator
! with a ramped loadshape) and don't fit the zone-distributed auth
! experiment shape.
!
! Usage: GRID_MODEL=/usr/app/examples/Run_IEEE123_ZTCARD.dss

! Load the base IEEE 123 model. `Compile` (vs `Redirect`) makes the
! ieee123/ subdir the working directory so the Master's relative
! Redirects (IEEELineCodes.DSS, IEEE123Loads.dss, IEEE123Regulators.DSS)
! resolve correctly.
Compile (ieee123/IEEE123Master.dss)

! ============================================================================
! PV/Temperature curves (shared by all PV systems, same as the IEEE 8500 +
! IEEE 37 PV wrappers — single source-of-shape for the experiment matrix)
! ============================================================================
New XYCurve.MyPvsT npts=4 xarray=[0 25 75 100] yarray=[1.2 1.0 0.8 0.6]
New XYCurve.MyEff npts=4 xarray=[.1 .2 .4 1.0] yarray=[.86 .9 .93 .97]
New Loadshape.MyIrrad npts=24 interval=1 mult=[0 0 0 0 0 0 0.1 .2 .3 .5 .8 .9 1.0 1.0 .99 .9 .7 .4 .1 0 0 0 0 0]
New Tshape.MyTemp npts=24 interval=1 temp=[25 25 25 25 25 25 25 25 35 40 45 50 60 60 55 40 35 30 25 25 25 25 25 25]

! ============================================================================
! PV portfolio — 15 sites × 75 kW = 1.125 MW total. Spread across phases
! and across the feeder by BFS depth from source bus 150. The data-init
! zone partitioner (BFS) will bucket these into the 5 control zones.
!
! Bus selection avoids 33/67/114/300 (PowerGym batteries). Each PV is on
! an existing single-phase primary bus; phase suffix matches the primary
! definition in IEEE123Loads.dss.
! ============================================================================

! ── Phase 1 sites (5) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
New Transformer.pv_up_9   phases=1 Xhl=5.75
~ wdg=1 bus=9.1   kV=2.4 kVA=100
~ wdg=2 bus=trafo_pv_9   kV=0.24 kVA=100
New PVSystem.PV_9   phases=1 bus1=trafo_pv_9   kV=0.24 kVA=100 irrad=0.98 Pmpp=75 temperature=25 PF=1 effcurve=Myeff P-TCurve=MyPvsT Daily=MyIrrad TDaily=MyTemp

New Transformer.pv_up_14  phases=1 Xhl=5.75
~ wdg=1 bus=14.1  kV=2.4 kVA=100
~ wdg=2 bus=trafo_pv_14  kV=0.24 kVA=100
New PVSystem.PV_14  phases=1 bus1=trafo_pv_14  kV=0.24 kVA=100 irrad=0.98 Pmpp=75 temperature=25 PF=1 effcurve=Myeff P-TCurve=MyPvsT Daily=MyIrrad TDaily=MyTemp

