! ── Zone-fleet sites (10, added 2026-09-15 for ztcard-stack #1270) ─────────
! The 15 sites above were placed "by BFS depth so the data-init zone
! partitioner distributes them across the 5 zones" (see header). That intent
! silently failed: the partitioner put 9 of 15 in zone 0, 2 each in zones 1/3/4
! and NONE in zone 2. A hand-placed list that must agree with a computed
! partition, with nothing checking it -- the same defect that moved the
! backbone-line lists three times (ztcard-stack #1236, #1244, #1255).
!
! Consequences it caused, both in the corpus before this was found:
!   * S7 der_aggregation dispatches a same-zone DER fleet, so the attack was
!     only ever expressible in zone 0. Benign coordinated dispatch picks a zone
!     uniformly, so it landed mostly in zones that could not field a fleet --
!     making "which zone" a shortcut separating attack from benign.
!   * Zone 2 owned no DER at all, so a fifth of the feeder was outside the
!     experiment entirely.
!
! These 10 bring every zone to >=4 DERs. Placement is still by hand and will
! drift again the moment the partition moves; what stops that is the assertion
! in data-init (_assert_every_zone_has_a_der_fleet), not this comment.
!
! Phases are taken from IEEE123Master.dss per bus, not assumed: buses 58, 69,
! 45, 73 and 112 are single-phase and mounting a PV on a phase they do not own
! would leave a floating node.

New Transformer.pv_up_58  phases=1 Xhl=5.75
~ wdg=1 bus=58.2   kV=2.4 kVA=100
~ wdg=2 bus=trafo_pv_58  kV=0.24 kVA=100
New PVSystem.PV_58  phases=1 bus1=trafo_pv_58  kV=0.24 kVA=100 irrad=0.98 Pmpp=75 temperature=25 PF=1 effcurve=Myeff P-TCurve=MyPvsT Daily=MyIrrad TDaily=MyTemp

New Transformer.pv_up_69  phases=1 Xhl=5.75
~ wdg=1 bus=69.1   kV=2.4 kVA=100
~ wdg=2 bus=trafo_pv_69  kV=0.24 kVA=100
New PVSystem.PV_69  phases=1 bus1=trafo_pv_69  kV=0.24 kVA=100 irrad=0.98 Pmpp=75 temperature=25 PF=1 effcurve=Myeff P-TCurve=MyPvsT Daily=MyIrrad TDaily=MyTemp

