! ============================================================================
! Re-establish voltage bases for the new PV step-up transformer secondaries so
! OpenDSS reports per-unit voltages correctly on the new buses. VoltageBases
! entries are line-to-line; the PV step-up windings are rated 0.24 kV
! line-to-NEUTRAL on a single-phase secondary (LL-equivalent 0.24*sqrt(3) =
! 0.415692 kV). Listing 0.24 made CalcVoltageBases snap those nodes to the
! nearest base of 0.48 instead, so a healthy 1.0 pu node read as 0.24/(0.48/sqrt(3)) =
! 0.866 pu. Measured before/after on this feeder: min node pu 0.853 -> 0.979,
! nodes under 0.95 pu 25 -> 0, matching the stock (no-PV) feeder's 0.979 floor.
! ============================================================================
Set VoltageBases = [4.16, 0.48, 0.415692]
CalcVoltageBases

! Solve a snapshot power flow so the PV systems initialize against the
! current load + regulator state. Mirrors the post-init solve in
! Run_IEEE8500_ZTCARD.dss.
Solve
